# Two jobs: keep the build context small, and keep deployment secrets out of an
# image that may end up in a registry.
#
# Patterns are matched against paths relative to the context root, so a bare
# `*.sqlite` would match `./fxa.sqlite` and nothing deeper.  Everything that has
# to match at any depth is written `**/`.

# 844 MB of upstream checkouts.  Gitignored, therefore invisible to review, and
# without this line every byte of it is uploaded to the daemon on every build.
resources/

.git/
.github/
.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.hypothesis/
.mypy_cache/
.claude/

# The development interpreter pin.  Copied into the build it would make uv look
# for the 3.12 that is not in the base image; the image's Python is chosen by
# the FROM line, which is the only place that choice should live.
.python-version

# Local deployment state — mirrors the block of the same name in .gitignore.
# `serve` reads all of these from /data at runtime; none of them belongs in a
# layer.  scripts/docker-smoke.sh asserts the built image contains no such path.
fxa.toml
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite-wal
**/*.sqlite-shm
signing-key.json
retired-key.json
deploy/nginx.conf

# Not needed to build the wheel.  `uv sync --no-editable` installs the project
# from src/ + pyproject.toml + uv.lock + README.md (pyproject names it), and the
# runtime stage receives only /app/.venv, so anything else is context weight.
tests/
scripts/
deploy/
docs/
plan.md
AUDIT.md
UPSTREAM.toml
fxa.example.toml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yaml
